## Example

On the compactified oriented four-sphere, take the smooth patchwise charge-one SU(2) BPST connection on the specified bundle with anti-Hermitian fundamental trace $\operatorname{tr}_{\mathbf2}(T_aT_b)=-\tfrac12\delta_{ab}$ and charge convention $\nu=-c_2(E_{\mathbf2})$. Assume this smooth finite-action connection has $F_A=*F_A$ and $\nu=1$, and that the self-dual action-bound and source-free Euler–Lagrange statements use the same normalization as the adopted Euclidean model. Then it is a classical instanton saddle with $S_E[A]=8\pi^2/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2$. If the model includes the dimensionless theta coupling, its formal single-saddle factor is $e^{-8\pi^2/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2+i\theta}$. The factor is not an evaluated continuum path integral.

## Example references

[Tong, §1.1.1, self-duality bound and charge-one solution](https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/tasi/instanton.pdf)

[Vandoren and van Nieuwenhuizen, §2, winding number, bound, and theta term](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0802.1862)

[Belavin, Polyakov, Schwartz, and Tyupkin, pp. 85–86, original charge-one solution](https://strings.itp.ac.ru/Papers/belavin1975.pdf)

## Facts & Assumptions

**Given:** The SU(2) Euclidean model of the assigned definition, $g_{\mathrm{YM}}>0$, the anti-Hermitian defining-representation trace, the stated charge convention, and the following planned inputs used only conditionally.

[A1] The coupling satisfies $g_{\mathrm{YM}}>0$, and $\theta$ is present only in the optional theta-deformed model.

[F1] The action is $S_E[A]=S_0[A]/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2$, where $S_0[A]=\tfrac12\int_M B(F_A\wedge *F_A)$. [[def-qftx-euclidean-yang-mills-sector]]

[F2] The optional sector phase is $e^{i\theta\nu}$, and the full expression is only a formal continuum sector notation without a measure, gauge fixing, determinant, or limit. [[def-qftx-euclidean-yang-mills-sector]]

[L1] The planned charge-one BPST example is to exhibit a smooth SU(2) connection on the compactified four-sphere, in a named gauge, with finite action, self-dual curvature, $\nu=1$ in the adopted orientation/trace convention, and the required patch transition. Its carrier and proof are absent in the current batch evidence; it is used here only as a conditional input. [[ex-qftx-su2-bpst-one-instanton]]

[L2] The planned theorem contract requires the $F^\pm$ action bound and its equality cases for the stated charge normalization, and the Bianchi implication to the source-free equation, but it does not record an exact coefficient. This example conditionally assumes the SU(2) convention of the assigned definition yields $S_0[A]\ge 8\pi^2|\nu|$, with equality when $F_A=\pm *F_A$. The carrier and proof are absent; the coefficient and trace match remain unresolved. [[thm-qftx-yang-mills-selfdual-action-bound]]

[L3] The planned physical Euler–Lagrange theorem is to vary the adopted curvature action through smooth compactly supported connection variations, using $\delta F_A=D_A\delta A$ and the invariant pairing, and obtain the source-free equation $D_A*F_A=0$. Its carrier and proof are absent in the current batch evidence; this is used only as the intended conditional physical interface. [[pthm-qftx-nonabelian-yang-mills-euler-lagrange]]

