 ## Example
 
-On the compactified oriented four-sphere, take the regular-gauge charge-one SU(2) BPST connection with anti-Hermitian fundamental trace $\operatorname{tr}_{\mathbf2}(T_aT_b)=-\tfrac12\delta_{ab}$ and charge convention $\nu=-c_2(E_{\mathbf2})$. Assume this smooth finite-action connection has $F_A=*F_A$ and $\nu=1$, and that the self-dual action-bound and source-free Euler–Lagrange statements use the same normalization as the adopted Euclidean model. Then it is a classical instanton saddle with $S_E[A]=8\pi^2/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2$. If the model includes the dimensionless theta coupling, its formal single-saddle factor is $e^{-8\pi^2/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2+i\theta}$. The factor is not an evaluated continuum path integral.
+Let $S^4=\{z\in\mathbb R^5:|z|=1\}$ have its unit round metric. Let $p_\infty$ be the point omitted by the north stereographic chart, let $p_0$ have north-chart coordinate $x=0$, and orient $S^4$ so $dx^1\wedge dx^2\wedge dx^3\wedge dx^4>0$. In the north chart put $r^2=\sum_{\mu=1}^4(x^\mu)^2$; the metric is $4(1+r^2)^{-2}\sum_\mu(dx^\mu)^2$. In the south chart put $y=x/r^2$; the metric is $4(1+|y|^2)^{-2}\sum_\mu(dy^\mu)^2$. Define $SU(2)=\{U\in M_2(\mathbb C):U^*U=I_2,\det U=1\}$. Use the Pauli matrices $\sigma_1=\begin{pmatrix}0&1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$, $\sigma_2=\begin{pmatrix}0&-i\\i&0\end{pmatrix}$, $\sigma_3=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&-1\end{pmatrix}$ and anti-Hermitian generators $T_a=-i\sigma_a/2$. Let $\epsilon_{ijk}$ be totally antisymmetric with $\epsilon_{123}=1$, set $\eta_{aij}=\epsilon_{aij}$, $\eta_{ai4}=\delta_{ai}$, $\bar\eta_{aij}=-\epsilon_{aij}$, and $\bar\eta_{ai4}=\delta_{ai}$ for $i,j\in\{1,2,3\}$, and extend both arrays antisymmetrically in their last two indices. For any $\rho>0$, put $u(x)=(x^4I_2-i x^j\sigma_j)/r$ on the overlap, and glue two trivial right $SU(2)$ bundles with local sections satisfying $s_S=s_Nu^{-1}$. The local connection potentials are
+
+$$A_N=\frac{2\eta_{a\mu\nu}x^\nu}{r^2+\rho^2}T_a\,dx^\mu,\qquad A_S=-\frac{2\rho^2\bar\eta_{a\mu\nu}y^\nu}{1+\rho^2|y|^2}T_a\,dy^\mu.$$
+
+On the overlap the potentials obey $A_S=\operatorname{Ad}_uA_N+u\,d(u^{-1})$, with the right-action section convention above. Use the conditional Euclidean action $S_E=(2g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2)^{-1}\int_{S^4}\kappa(F\wedge *F)$ with $\kappa(X,Y)=-2\operatorname{tr}_{\mathbf2}(XY)$, and the compactified charge $\nu=-(8\pi^2)^{-1}\int_{S^4}\operatorname{tr}_{\mathbf2}(F\wedge F)$, for fixed $g_{\mathrm{YM}}>0$. For this specified smooth two-chart connection, the charge is $\nu=1$, the curvature is self-dual, and $S_E=8\pi^2/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2$; it is a classical instanton saddle. If the formal sector expression includes the dimensionless theta coupling $\theta$, the corresponding formal single-saddle factor is $e^{-8\pi^2/g_{\mathrm{YM}}^2+i\theta}$. This factor is not an evaluated continuum path integral.
 
